dashboard='## Quant & Market Dashboard\n\n**Data status / overnight liquidity:** Futures direction is a reported snapshot in story 3, not a current executable order book. Overnight futures/ETF spreads, depth and volume, funding/repo and Treasury bid/ask signals were not independently verified. No current funding or Treasury-market signal was independently verified; no liquidity direction is inferred from missing data.\n\n**Volatility regime — stressed; medium confidence.** YCharts’ historical series reports November 20 prior-close VIX of 35.89, versus 28.44 on November 19. These are completed-session observations, not live Monday readings. Editorial thresholds: below 15 low, 15–20 moderate, 20–30 high, 30 or above stressed. This classification does not establish liquidity stress or today’s SPY/QQQ options surface. Source: https://ycharts.com/indicators/vix_volatility_index\n\n**Factors — performance unavailable, no rankings:**\n\n| Exposure | ETF proxy | One session | Four weeks |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Momentum | MTUM | Unavailable | Unavailable |\n| Value | VLUE | Unavailable | Unavailable |\n| Quality | QUAL | Unavailable | Unavailable |\n| Size | IWM | Unavailable | Unavailable |\n| Growth | IWF | Unavailable | Unavailable |\n| Low volatility | SPLV | Unavailable | Unavailable |\n\nIntended latest completed common-session end: **November 20**; preceding session **November 19**. Four-week target start freshly calculated as **October 23**, exactly 28 calendar days before November 20. Actual common start, comparable prices and adjustments: **unverified; no substitute date used**. Required basis is split-adjusted closing-price return excluding distributions, applying in-window splits once and excluding out-of-window actions. Alpha Vantage’s standard terms provide personal non-commercial use unless otherwise agreed in writing; publication permission for this repository and newsletter use was not verified. No Alpha Vantage prices, corporate actions or derived returns are exported. A publication-cleared comparable alternative was not verified. ETF proxies are not pure factors. Terms: https://www.alphavantage.co/terms_of_service/\n\n**SPY/QQQ and options execution:** Monday cash opening auction: **8:30 a.m. CST**; U.S. flash PMI: **8:45 a.m. CST**, fifteen minutes later. Treat opening-gap fills and the PMI reaction as separate event windows. Wednesday November 25 GDP/PCE: **7:30 a.m. CST**. Thanksgiving November 26 closed; November 27 cash closes **noon CST**, eligible options **12:15 p.m. CST**; check contract and venue. Reconcile Friday monthly-expiry exercise and assignment. Dealer gamma sign and remaining strike concentrations are unverified; avoid unsupported pin assumptions. Use limits and staged participation; compare spread, depth and slippage with time-of-day baselines. Stale Friday options marks, midpoint fills without size and thin premarket prints are liquidity traps. Holiday-thin trading is a risk, not a measured condition today. Calendar sources: https://www.pmi.spglobal.com/Public/Home/PDF/UK_Rel_Dates ; https://www.bea.gov/news/schedule ; https://www.nyse.com/trade/hours-calendars\n\n**Microstructure implications / research watchlist:** Gate participation on fresh quotes, size and spread relative to baseline; stress partial fills and liquidity withdrawal. A futures rebound does not establish improved execution liquidity. Monitor SPY, QQQ, IWM, MTUM, VLUE, QUAL, IWF, SPLV, TLT, NVDA, MU, CRWD and ZS. This is a research watchlist, not a recommendation to trade.\n\n### DRL Improvements for the MATLAB System\n\n- Enforce exposure, turnover, drawdown and capital-preservation limits outside the learned policy; log every veto and breach.\n- Reward net performance after commissions, spread and impact, penalizing tail losses and unstable turnover. Simulate latency, partial fills and liquidity withdrawal.\n- Use purged walk-forward evaluation with embargoes, frozen final holdouts and regime-stratified stress tests. Compare against cash and simple baselines; retain failed trials and execution-cost sensitivity results.\n\n### Model Hygiene\n\nFit transforms only within training folds. Use point-in-time constituents and release timestamps to prevent survivorship, leakage and look-ahead bias. Version corporate actions and apply adjustments once. Reject stale, crossed or zero-size options quotes. Count all configurations, control multiple testing, and monitor calibration and drift; do not select retraining rules on the final holdout.\n\n### MATLAB Optimization Patterns\n\n- Align timezone-aware timetables before vectorizing features and returns; keep observation dates separate from publication timestamps.\n- Profile before parallel Bayesian optimization. Freeze objective inputs and random streams, and archive trial order; parallel timing can still prevent exact reproducibility.\n- Keep data, reward, independent risk gates and execution modules separate. Use GPUs for suitable large tensor workloads; benchmark transfer overhead and minimize host/device transfers.\n\nTechnical references: https://www.mathworks.com/help/stats/parallel_bayesian_optimization.html ; https://www.mathworks.com/help/reinforcement-learning/ug/train-reinforcement-learning-agents.html ; https://www.mathworks.com/help/parallel-computing/measure-and-improve-gpu-performance.html\n\n**High-value quant research question:** Do physics-inspired covariance features improve net portfolio outcomes beyond equally tuned HAR-RV and LSTM baselines in a fresh ETF universe? Use nested walk-forward ablations, identical decision timestamps, turnover costs and multiple-testing controls. Worth testing because a new null result suggests complexity may add maintenance and overfitting risk without measurable economic benefit; replication could establish whether that finding transfers.\n'

